
# Rust
./target/
./target/*
./target/flycheck/*
**/target/
Cargo.lock.bak
*.pdb

# Beads / Dolt files (added by bd init)
.dolt/
*.db
.beads-credential-key
.beads/proxieddb/

# KOPITIAM Semantic Runtime per-project state (local session memory)
.kopitiam/

# token-harness local corpus: machine-specific list of local PDF paths
# (by path only, never copied in -- see scripts/token-harness.corpus.example).
scripts/token-harness.corpus

# Vendored reference sources for translation (not part of the Pure Rust Core;
# local-only, NEVER committed — see README.md's "Scientific Translation" plan).
# `vendor/` (no leading slash) matches a directory named `vendor` at ANY depth,
# so every reference dropin (crates/*/vendor, apps/*/vendor, ...) is ignored.
vendor/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Model weights and anything else fetched from the network
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Never commit weights. They are hundreds of MB, they are somebody else's
# redistribution to make, and git cannot store them usefully — a .gguf is
# already-compressed binary, so every re-fetch is a fresh unmergeable blob in
# history forever. The netfetch tests pull into the XDG model store, but a
# stray copy in the worktree (a hand-dropped BYO file, a `--out` typo) must not
# be committable by accident.
*.gguf
*.GGUF
*.safetensors
*.traineddata
# Scratch dir the netfetch tests use when pointed away from the XDG store.
/.netfetch-models/
